{{also|Вера}}
==Russian==

===Etymology===
Old Church Slavonic [[вѣра]] identical to {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*věra}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*weh₁ro-||true}}.  Cognate with Ukrainian [[віра]], Bulgarian [[вяра]], Slovenian ''[[vera]]'', Polish ''[[wiara]]''.  The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{term/t|la|vērus}} and German {{term|wahr|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvʲerə/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-вера.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|tr=véra|g=f}}

#[[faith]], [[belief]], [[trust]]
#[[religion]]

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-а-1|вер|ве́р}}

====Related terms====
* [[верить]]
* [[верование]]
* [[веровать]]
* [[верный]]
* [[верующий]]
* [[неверующий]]

